GenAISA Code Conversion – How I Did It (Datavant Example)
Oct 23, 2026 · @don
I converted the Datavant MBR+PROV job (RAA-DATAVANTPROV-ETL, job 780009056) to the GenAISA framework and tested it end to end in UAT, including dispatch. These are the steps I followed, with my actual files as examples, plus the issues I hit so you don't have to.
My job for reference: GEN_AI_SA_ID 005, Jira RBICA-14353, LOB MCR. The converted output in UAT matched the old Scala run row for row.
The overall flow:
1. Collect the source files for your job.
2. Set up the conversion folder and run Devin.
3. Review what Devin generates and fix the config.
4. Upload the SQL to S3.
5. Insert the config rows through the adhoc job.
6. Run main_refactored.py on a cluster.
7. Verify the files and tables against the old job.
8. Set up and test dispatch (Lambda config).
